  THE ROUTE RELATION DOES NOT CLOSE AT 6 — IT CLOSES AT 10, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE
  POINT OF SPLITTING THE KNOB (PDS-D480). Write-routed climbs 24/28/36/45/52/57 across
  depths 1..6 and KEEPS CLIMBING past it: 62/64/70/81/81/81/81 at depths
  7/8/9/10/12/14/16. It goes flat at 10 — write 81 / read 16 / unrouted 3, IDENTICAL at
  depth(s) 12, 14, 16 — because the bfs seen-set makes the reachable set a finite
  closure and the route set is MONOTONE in the budget. Until wave 35's two dead seams
  in raw_calls/1 were repaired (a capture, and a `mod.f(...)` variable module head)
  the table went flat at 6 instead, and this census read that artefact as a property
  of the code. @route_depth is 10; ROUTE-DEPTH-IS-CLOSURE below reds if it stops matching.

  NEITHER WRITE FIGURE MAY BE QUOTED ALONE. THE PAIR IS THE UNIT:
      @evidence_depth 6   write 57  ·  POST-READ 21   <- the classification this census SHIPS
