SHAPE (PDS-D453 taxonomy — six shapes, or UNCLASSIFIED; never a guess)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  READ THE POST-READ COUNT AS A CEILING, not a clean bill of health. Its evidence is
  line order — a Repo READ below a Repo WRITE inside the writing function — which is
  NECESSARY and NOT SUFFICIENT: this lens cannot prove the read is OF THE ROW that
  was written. `select:` inside the update query is the one spelling it CAN prove.
  Wave 34 confirms each one by hand; a POST-READ here is a candidate, not a verdict.

  EVERY POST-READ BELOW IS ADMISSIBLE, NONE IS PROVEN HONEST. ARM 1
  (has_select_in_update?/1) now proves the `select:` sits ON THE QUERY THAT IS
  UPDATED — it did not before, and any writing function that also ran a read query
  with `select:` manufactured a true positive. It still does NOT prove the caller
  SPENDS the selected row on the value it prints, nor that the caller even takes the
  branch the evidence was read on. Both refusals are DERIVED and NAMED in `THE
  `select:` EVIDENCE, TAKEN APART` above, over this corpus, rather than conceded
  here in prose: BlockOps.fenced_paper_update/4 selects the saved row and its caller
  binds it, spends it on side effects, and prints a PRE-WRITE rev.

