  DERIVATION PARTITION of the 148 status_only_receipt row(s) — what the
  receipt ACTUALLY renders, DERIVED this run over 116 distinct {module, action} pair(s)
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Clause A of the class prose ("reaches no `ok: true` receipt this lens can see")
  holds for every row by construction. Clause B ("claims success by STATUS alone")
  is a claim about the CODE, and this is the measurement of it:

    store_derived                114
                                 the receipt renders a value bound out of
                                 an `{:ok, _}` payload whose producing
                                 call is NOT read-shaped — the response
                                 describes the row the write returned.
                                 Clause B of the wave-38 prose is FALSE of
                                 these rows.
    reread_receipt                 8
                                 the receipt renders an `{:ok, _}` payload
                                 from a READ-shaped call
                                 (get_/fetch_/list_/projection/...). The
                                 write's own return was discarded and the
                                 store was asked again; honest about the
                                 store, but one round trip away from the
                                 write it claims.
    request_echo                   4
                                 the receipt renders values bound in the
                                 action's own HEAD — request params. It
                                 describes what the CALLER SENT, not what
                                 the store holds: the species #9114 found
                                 six of on DELETE verbs, where a lying
                                 receipt costs a person the most.
    control_flow_gated_literal     2
                                 the body is a CONSTANT (a redirect or a
                                 flash whose text carries no bound value)
                                 reached only inside an `{:ok, _}` branch
                                 whose payload is discarded. Describing
                                 the store by value: ZERO. Describing the
                                 request: ZERO. Neither derived nor an
                                 echo — success is asserted by CONTROL
                                 FLOW.
    literal_only                   3
                                 the response body carries no bound value
                                 at all and no discarded `{:ok, _}` gate
                                 this pass could attribute — a
                                 204/empty-body or a fixed literal. This
                                 IS wave 38's clause B, and this class is
                                 how many rows actually deserved it.
    residual_helper_assembled     10
                                 RESIDUAL, NOT DECIDED: the action's own
                                 body contains no response call — the
                                 receipt is assembled inside a helper.
                                 Bindings join across the hop and this
                                 pass declines to follow them rather than
                                 guess.
    residual_onehop_unattributed   7
                                 RESIDUAL, NOT DECIDED: a response call
                                 exists and renders bound values, but none
                                 of them trace to an `{:ok, _}` payload OR
                                 to the action's head — they are bound by
                                 an intermediate this pass does not
                                 attribute.
    residual_undecided             0
                                 RESIDUAL, NOT DECIDED: no response call
                                 and no local helper call in the action's
