  WHAT THIS PARTITION CANNOT SEE (its own blind shapes, printed with it)
    · SHADOWING IS NOT MODELLED. dvars/1 is a NAME SET, so a name rebound between
      its `{:ok, _}` binding and the render still reads as store-derived here.
    · THE DENOMINATOR IS AN UPPER BOUND. The JUDGED relation upstream is ONE HOP
      (dispose_routed/4 says so): a receipt two helpers deep reads as EXCLUDED and
      lands in this partition rather than in JUDGED, so some rows below are not
      status-only at all — they are judged receipts the relation could not reach.
    · reread_receipt IS DECIDED BY THE PRODUCING CALL NAME, which is a string test.
      Every row above prints that name, so the verdict is auditable prose rather
      than a silent filter — check any row against its source and this pass loses.
    · WHICH REGION DECIDED THE ROW IS MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED. success_scopes/1 reads
      the `{:ok, _}` BRANCH where one carries a response call — 109 row(s) here.
      The other 39 fall back to the WHOLE def body (no attributable success scope),
      where an ERROR-branch payload can decide the verdict; 0 row(s) have no body at
      all. And a def with two unrelated success scopes contributes BOTH — the union
      is taken, never proven benign.
    · A VALUE THE PLUG ALREADY LOADED IS INVISIBLE. dvars/1 drops `conn`, so a
      receipt built from `conn.assigns[:document]` — a store value fetched before
      the action ran — contributes no var and can read as literal_only.
    · A REDIRECT'S `to:` IS NOT A PAYLOAD. Recording it would let a redirect built
      from a caller-supplied id read as store-derived.
    · A HOP ARGUMENT THAT IS A CALL IS ATTRIBUTED ON ITS OWN RETURN, AND FOR SOME OF
      THEM THAT IS A GUESS. hop_arg_shape/1 reads the argument's TOP-LEVEL shape, so
      `stamp_response(conn, Keys.pause(id, ...))` now attributes producer `pause`
      instead of substituting the head var `id` into the parameter pattern
      `{:ok, key}` — that substitution is what made the TicketKeys rows class
      request_echo on a value that descends from the write. But 27 hop argument
      position(s) are calls whose OWN inputs trace to NEITHER an `{:ok, _}` payload
      NOR the head: their producer is MINTED from the call name alone, on no
      provenance at all. 3 of them sit on the substitution the join CHOSE — that
      is the PROXY, and it OVERSTATES its own name: it counts a mint anywhere in the
      winning substitution, including parameters whose vars never reach the rendered
      payload at all. 0 of those positions ACTUALLY DECIDE the printed class: the
      minted parameter's vars are intersected with the payload_vars the winning
      callee was classified on, and a name the callee REBINDS itself is excluded
      because the producer that lands in `used` is then the callee's, not the mint's.
      NO mint decides a printed class this run. Both numbers are kept: the proxy is the
      guessing SURFACE, the exact one is the guessing EFFECT, and a slice that
      printed only the proxy would report an exposure it cannot show. This is a
      COUNTED exposure rather than a class of its own (PDS-D618): the numbers are
      printed every run, so the day a mint decides a row it moves in public.
    · FIELD ACCESS AND SUBSCRIPTS ARE NOT CALLS, and are excluded BY SHAPE rather
      than by name — 1 field-access and 5 subscript hop argument position(s)
